# Derived by hand from Semantics ch. 4 ("A block whose last line is a bind or a `let` returns `unit`"; `ignore` stands as the left side of a bind) and ruling TC (places counted as built): loud builds the clause's label at 0 and "after" at 1; soft's clause builds nothing, so "after" stands at 0.
test loud

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Label(text="loud")
    1: Ui.Label(text="after")

test soft

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Label(text="after")
